/**
 * SVG Icon Library for KeymapViewer
 * Provides SVG rendering with WebFont fallback support
 *
 * Implementation Strategy:
 * - Each icon has SVG definition + WebFont fallback
 * - SVG rendering is optional; WebFont always available
 * - Failed SVG renders silently fall back to WebFont
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * 🚀 ADDING NEW SVG ICONS - Automated Process
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * DO NOT manually add SVG entries. Use the automation script instead:
 *
 *   bash scripts/add-svg-icon.sh [--dry-run] KEYCODE [KEYCODE...]
 *
 * Examples:
 *   bash scripts/add-svg-icon.sh KC_STOP KC_HELP
 *   bash scripts/add-svg-icon.sh --dry-run KC_MAIL           (preview changes)
 *
 * The script automatically:
 * 1. Extracts icon name from js/keymap-dictionary.js
 * 2. Searches FluentUI System Icons repository (/tmp/fluentui-system-icons)
 * 3. Retrieves the corresponding 24px filled SVG
 * 4. Generates proper SVG_ICONS entry with metadata
 * 5. Adds entry to this file with correct formatting
 * 6. Returns JSON output for verification
 *
 * Requirements:
 * - keymap-dictionary.js must have fluent: value for the keycode
 * - FluentUI System Icons repo must be cloned at /tmp/fluentui-system-icons
 * - Bash environment (Git Bash, WSL, native Linux, macOS)
 *
 * ============================================================================
 */

